            <ArticleTitle>[Adnexal torsion in a six-year-old girl].</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">V02170123</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Adnexal torsion is a rare condition but should be considered in any female patient with acute-onset lower abdominal pain regardless of age. In this case report a six-year-old girl presented with four days of lower abdominal pain. On suspicion of acute appendicitis a diagnostic laparoscopy was performed and showed left-sided adnexal torsion. The ovary was detorsed, and one third of the ovary was resected. A transabdominal ultrasound three months after surgery showed no signs of pathology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
